Ludwig walks quickly next to me.
We are on our way to a local dog forest.
The sun is shining nicely this afternoon.
He pulls a little eagerly on the leash.
"Wait," I say firmly to him.
"You must walk nicely."
We finally arrive at the large gate.
The dog forest is fenced and completely safe.
We go in, and I close the gate behind us.
I crouch down and look at him.
I slowly unclip the leash from his collar.
"Now you may run freely," I say with a smile.
He looks happily at me and runs off quickly.
I find a good stick on the ground.
"Look here, Ludwig!" I shout and show it to him.
I throw the stick far away in among the trees.
"Fetch it!" I say loudly.
He runs over to the stick and takes it in his mouth.
"Come back," I call and clap my hands.
He is really a good dog.
